    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe core logic is well-placed and idiomatic: `isCityAtCapacity` correctly reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity` private helper (no duplication, same case-insensitive counting as the customer-code sequence), and the controller guard clause mirrors the adjacent `isTelephoneInUse`/`isHouseholdInUse` CONFLICT checks exactly. The interface method is well-documented. Two minor structural nits:\n\n- **Constant placement breaks the class's own convention.** Every other field/constant in `ClinicServiceImpl` is declared at the top of the class (lines 50\u201355). The new `private static final long CITY_CAPACITY = 50L;` is instead buried at line 377, mid-class between the `normalizeTelephone` helper and `isCityAtCapacity`. Move it up with the other class-level members so it reads naturally.\n\n- **Method placement is somewhat arbitrary.** `isCityAtCapacity` is inserted between the household/telephone normalize helpers and `findOwnerByLastName`. It would sit more naturally next to the helper it depends on (`countOwnersInCity`, line 288) or beside the sibling validation method `isTelephoneInUse` (line 297), grouping the capacity logic with related code rather than splitting the normalize helpers from the query methods.",
